      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_MeshType_Header",
      "Text": "Mesh Type"
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_MeshType_Header_TT",
      "Text": "The Havok shape the collision is built as. Compressed meshes are what the game's own collision uses, and carry a collision material. Extern meshes store the triangles uncompressed, without materials."
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGeneratorMeshType_Compressed",
      "Text": "Compressed Mesh"
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGeneratorMeshType_Extern",
      "Text": "Extern Mesh"
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_Material_Header",
      "Text": "Collision Material"
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_Material_Header_TT",
      "Text": "The collision material is the surface the generated triangles get: a HitMtrlParam row, which sets the footstep sounds, hit effects and swamp or water behaviour, plus an optional property. FLVER meshes whose material is named in the OBJ2HKX style, hkm_Name or hkm_Name_Property (for example hkm_Cobblestone_Safe1), use that material instead; the mesh list shows which material each mesh will get."
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_Material_Input_TT",
      "Text": "The material ID that is written: the surface row plus the property in the hundreds, for example 429 is surface 29 with Slide1. Type an ID here to use a value the lists above don't offer."
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_Material_From_Current",
      "Text": "Use Current Material"
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_Material_From_Current_TT",
      "Text": "Sets the material ID to the material of the collision shape being replaced."
    },
    {
      "Key": "HAVOK_CollisionGen_Material_From_Current_None",
      "Text": "The current collision shape has no collision material."
    },
    {
